      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course! For the word \"zoo,\" the /z/ sound is formed with voiced alveolar fricative, meaning the vocal cords vibrate when air is forced between them. On the other hand, for the word \"sue,\" the /s/ sound is an unvoiced alveolar fricative; your vocal cords don't vibrate at all. It's the presence or absence of vocal cord vibration that sets them apart.",
